#!/bin/bash
# Ubuntu : redémarrage après mise à jour (sans vérification pacman du noyau).
if [[ -f /var/run/reboot-required || -f $HOME/.local/state/omarchy/reboot-required ]]; then
  gum confirm "Une mise à jour demande un redémarrage. Redémarrer ?" && { omarchy-system-reboot; exit 0; }
fi
running=$(readlink /proc/$(pgrep -x Hyprland | head -1)/exe 2>/dev/null)
[[ $running == *"(deleted)"* ]] && gum confirm "Hyprland a été mis à jour. Redémarrer ?" && { omarchy-system-reboot; exit 0; }
for file in "$HOME"/.local/state/omarchy/restart-*-required; do
  [[ -f $file ]] || continue
  service=$(basename "$file" | sed 's/restart-\(.*\)-required/\1/'); rm -f "$file"; "omarchy-restart-$service" || true
done
echo -e "\e[32m\nRestarting shell\e[0m"; omarchy-restart-shell || true
